    <item>
      <title>Sweden Gives Hope to Real Conservatives Everywhere</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-09-30/sweden-gives-hope-to-real-conservatives-everywhere</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">e9855d883fce7498b4365498</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:00:13 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Ulf Kristersson’s Moderates, who’ve spent four years leading Sweden’s governing coalition, did what voters wanted. The center-right party got growth going: It’s expected to be 2.5% for 2026 and 2027, remarkable for a European nation. Inflation is 0.3%, and — of greater importance to plenty of Swedes — asylum applications this year will be the lowest since 1985. They’ve even started building nuclear power plants again.</description>
      <dc:creator>Mihir Sharma</dc:creator>
